{"term":"skim","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1c0dfc509bb20e6f5a","definition":"To pass lightly; to glide along in an even, smooth course; to glide along near the surface.","example":"Not so when swift Camilla scours the plain, / Flies o'er the unbending corn, and skims along the main.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["cream-skim","overskim","reskim","semi-skimmed","skimboard","skimboarding","skimmability","skimmable","skimmed milk","skimmer","skimmy","skim off","skim over","skim-read","skim through"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7fad130c267f2904b5","definition":"To pass near the surface of; to brush the surface of; to glide swiftly along the surface of.","example":"Homer describes Mercury as flinging himself from the top of Olympus, and skimming the surface of the ocean.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["cream-skim","overskim","reskim","semi-skimmed","skimboard","skimboarding","skimmability","skimmable","skimmed milk","skimmer","skimmy","skim off","skim over","skim-read","skim through"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:26048d42af1b80a4a5","definition":"To hasten along with superficial attention.","example":"They skim over a science in a very night superficial survey.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cream-skim","overskim","reskim","semi-skimmed","skimboard","skimboarding","skimmability","skimmable","skimmed milk","skimmer","skimmy","skim off","skim over","skim-read","skim through"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"